# Professional Linguistic Encyclopedia: Tabular UI & Layout Fix

The Linguistic Encyclopedia (Annotated, Disputed, Abbreviations) has been professionalized with a high-fidelity tabular interface and administrative auditing.

## 1. Professional Tabular Interface
- **Modern Grid**: Replaced card-based grids with a structured `<table>` for high-density document management.
- **Trilingual Columns**: English, Russian, and Uzbek columns are clearly separated with dedicated styling.
- **Context/Note Column**: Display description or expansion for annotated terms and abbreviations.

## 2. Advanced Multi-Column Filtering
- **Real-time Search**: Each column (EN, RU, UZ, Note) has its own search input.
- **Combined Logic**: Multiple filters can be combined to find specific terminology within large databases.

## 3. Administrative Audit Tracking
- **Role-Aware Display**:
  - **Regular Users**: See a clean 5-column table (EN, RU, UZ, Note, Actions).
  - **Administrators**: See an enhanced 7-column table with **Author** (Name/Email) and **Timestamp** for full accountability.
> [!IMPORTANT]
> The Author and Timestamp columns are automatically populated from the system's authentication layer.

## 4. UI/UX Refinements
- **Sidebar Fix**: Resolved the duplication issue by consolidating layout wrappers.
- **Interactive Modals**: Enhanced the add/edit modal to be category-aware, providing the correct fields for each linguistic group.
- **Micro-animations**: Added fade-in transitions and hover effects for a premium feel.

## Verification
- [x] Duplicate sidebar removed.
